 50  48 |
 51  49 |Two diagrams that reach a tie in the layout engine's block ordering, and so
 52  50 |pin the vendored `ascii-dag` fix (see `crates/ascii-dag/VENDORED.md`). A
 53  51 |subgraph's nodes are grouped into blocks, and the blocks are ordered by their
 54  52 |members' average position; when two blocks tie, an unfixed engine resolves the
 55  53 |tie from `HashMap` iteration and lays the diagram out differently from one
 56  54 |process to the next. Both diagrams below tie, so a regression here is a
 57  55 |flapping snapshot rather than a stable wrong picture:
 58  55 |
